				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\mathrm{SI}} = \frac{{\root {n} \of {{\mathop {\prod }\nolimits_{i = 1}^n {\mathrm{Cytotoxic}}_i}}}}{{\root {m} \of {{\mathop {\prod }\nolimits_{j = 1}^m {\mathrm{Antibacterial}}_j}}}},$$\end{document}SI=∏i=1nCytotoxicin∏j=1mAntibacterialjm,where n is the number of cytotoxic assays with different cells and m is the number of antimicrobial assays with different bacteria. For values higher than the maximum concentration tested, it was assumed twofold the maximum tested value (e.g. if the value is higher than 100, it was considered as 200)56.
